  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM - Ukraine Kakhovka dam - 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The breach of the Kakhovka Dam in Ukraine in June 2023 led to the depletion of the Kakhovka Reservoir and massive flooding, causing significant infrastructural damage. Homes, businesses, and community infrastructure have been devastated, compounding the challenges faced by a population already affected by ongoing war. With the reservoir&apos;s capacity reduced by 70 per cent, areas including Dnipropetrovsk, Zaporizhzhia, Mykolaiv, and Kherson regions are grappling with both water shortages and impacts of flooding. Water supply infrastructure was highly damaged and in affected regions, a substantial portion of the population has faced dire consequences due to the loss of access to piped water. Homes, businesses, and community infrastructure have been devastated, compounding the challenges faced by a population already affected by ongoing war. Through support from the Government of Canada, IOM is providing mid-term solutions such as clean drinking water and housing repairs while providing essential relief items, targeting 45,600 individuals in need.</narrative>
  </description>
